        {
          "id": "scm_call1440_thin_cirrus",
          "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run (GNU real32 build, dt = 60 s, 59 layers, p_top = 177.6 hPa so NBUF = 44 buffer layers, mp=6 ra_lw=1 ra_sw=1 sf_sfclay=1 sf_surface=1 bl_pbl=1) dumped by the instrumented fork ctessum-claude/WRF@e42a269 (module_esm_dump hooks in RRTMLWRAD and after RTRN inside SUBROUTINE RRTM of phys/module_ra_rrtm.F). RRTM has no standalone real64 driver, so every expected value is the real32 in-model value of MM5ATM/SETCOEF (PAVEL, TAVEL, PZ, TZ, COLDRY, COLH2O, COLCO2, COLN2O, COLCH4, COLO2, CLDFRAC, TAUCLOUD, TBOUND, SEMISS) and the tolerance contract is rel 1e-5. Inputs are the dumped RRTMLWRAD arguments of tile column 1 (p8w, t8w, p3d, t3d, qv..qs, cldfra3d, dz8w, bottom-up) and the scalars co2vmr, n2ovmr, ch4vmr, tsk, emiss. Measured mismatch over the four regimes: pz <= 3e-5 hPa (the real32 Pa -> hPa division), pavel/tavel/tz <= 1.4e-6 relative, coldry and the column amounts <= 7.6e-6 relative (the dominant term is the real32 rounding of the level pressures, 6e-5 hPa on the O(6 hPa) layer thickness), taucloud <= 7e-11, cldfrac exact. Column assertions are Linf_error with abs tolerances of about 1e-5 of each field's column maximum (pz, pavel 1e-2 hPa; tz, tavel 3e-3 K; coldry 6e18 cm^-2; colh2o 2e-4, colco2 3e-5, coln2o 2e-8, colch4 1e-7 cm^-2; taucloud 1e-8; cldfrac, colo2 0); the spot checks at the lowest model layer, the top model layer, the first buffer layer and the top buffer layer use rel 2e-5 for the column amounts (twice the contract, for the real32 level-pressure rounding just described) and rel 1e-5 otherwise. Identities on the inputs (tbound, semiss) use rel 1e-9. Regime: call 1440 (07:00 UTC), thin ice cloud (qi <= 6.7e-8) in layers 55-59, tsk = 278.4 K. Ozone (added 2026-09-06, dump scm_ref2_1440.json, which the rebuilt fork wrote for the identical SCM run): colo3 is compared with SETCOEF's COLO3 (Linf abs 1e-7 on a column maximum of 6.5e-3, spot checks rel 1e-5 at layers 59-103 where the column is above 1e-3 of its maximum; the lowest layers hold 5e-8 kg/kg with a 6e-4 relative real32 error from the 970 hPa interface pressures) and the climatological mixing ratio o3_clim with WKL(3)/(COLDRY amdo) at the same layers; the NumPy replica of O3DATA on MM5ATM's shifted interval agrees with the dump to 2.5e-6 relative (real32), the unshifted own-layer mean differs by 27 %, which pins the one-layer shift (FORTRAN_BUGS.md B5).",
