        {
          "id": "scm_call396_zero_fraction_override",
          "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run (GNU real32 build, dt = 60 s, 59 layers, p_top = 177.6 hPa so NBUF = 44 buffer layers, mp=6 ra_lw=1 ra_sw=1 sf_sfclay=1 sf_surface=1 bl_pbl=1) dumped by the instrumented fork ctessum-claude/WRF (module_esm_dump hooks in RRTMLWRAD and after RTRN inside SUBROUTINE RRTM of phys/module_ra_rrtm.F; dump scm_cloud_396.json, written by the same em_scm_xy run re-executed for 8 h with the cloudy calls added to ESM_DUMP_CALLS; the re-run reproduces the archived call 120 dump bit-for-bit, so it is the same trajectory). RRTM has no standalone real64 driver, so every expected value is the real32 in-model value of MM5ATM/SETCOEF (PAVEL, TAVEL, PZ, TZ, COLDRY, COLH2O, COLCO2, COLN2O, COLCH4, COLO2, CLDFRAC, TAUCLOUD, COLO3, TBOUND, SEMISS) and the tolerance contract is rel 1e-5. Inputs are the dumped RRTMLWRAD arguments of tile column 1 (p8w, t8w, p3d, t3d, qv..qs, cldfra3d, dz8w, bottom-up) and the scalars co2vmr, n2ovmr, ch4vmr, tsk, emiss. Column assertions are Linf_error with abs tolerances of about 1e-5 of each field's column maximum (pz, pavel 1e-2 hPa; tz, tavel 3e-3 K; coldry 6e18 cm^-2; colh2o 2e-4, colco2 3e-5, coln2o 2e-8, colch4 1e-7 cm^-2; colo3 1e-7; cldfrac and colo2 exactly 0), the spot checks at the lowest model layer, the top model layer, the first buffer layer and the top buffer layer use rel 2e-5 for the column amounts and rel 1e-5 otherwise, and identities on the inputs (tbound, semiss) use rel 1e-9. This regime is one of the four added on 2026-09-06 to cover MM5ATM's cloud block (phys/module_ra_rrtm.F:4252-4255): TAUCLOUD(L) = ABCW CLWP + ABICE CIWP + ABRN PLWP + ABSN PIWP on the model layers and zero on the buffer layers, and the overcast override IF (TAUCLOUD > 0.01) CLDFRC = 1, which replaces the diagnosed cloud fraction of every optically thicker layer by 1 and is the reason RTRN can only ever see 0 < CLDFRAC < 1 in a layer whose cloud optical depth is at or below 0.01. Regime: ZERO-FRACTION OVERRIDE. Call 396, 22:18 UTC (15:52 LST). Layer 51 is the only dumped case in the run where the diagnosed CLDFRA is exactly 0 and TAUCLOUD = 0.01072 nevertheless exceeds the threshold, so MM5ATM hands RTRN a fully overcast layer (CLDFRAC = 1) that the cloud-fraction diagnosis called cloud-free -- the clearest demonstration that the override is on TAUCLOUD alone (FORTRAN_BUGS.md N58). Layers 52-54 are overridden from 0.0969, 0.171, 0.181 (TAUCLOUD 0.0301, 0.0256, 0.0164), layer 55 keeps CLDFRA = 0.0368 (TAUCLOUD = 0.00229) and layers 56, 57, 59 are diagnosed overcast. tsk = 284.44 K. Measured mismatch: pz and pavel to Linf 2.9e-5 hPa, tz to 2.9e-5 K and tavel to 2.2e-5 K, coldry to 1.0e18 cm^-2 and the column amounts to 3.2e-6 relative (colh2o Linf 5.3e-5, colco2 3.9e-6, coln2o 3.3e-9, colch4 1.8e-8, colo3 2.7e-8 cm^-2), CLDFRAC exactly -- including the zero-fraction layer 51 that the override turns into an overcast one -- and TAUCLOUD to Linf 1.0e-9 on a column maximum of 0.0301, so taucloud uses abs 2e-8 (20x the measured floor).",
